# Product / content UX laws

## Instagram daily interview questions

- Source of truth: `documents/instagram-interview-question-guideline.md`. Update that file in place. Do not fork copies.
- On-screen question body is 10–28 words (sweet spot 18–26). Three spoken beats: situation, constraint, decision. Interviewers do not ask one line. Helper 4–9. Stakes hook 7–11. CTA 2–8.
- Frame is a fork in the road. Caption teaches. Never put the answer on the frame.
- Confuse them. Do not make them look dumb. No quiz-gotchas, no 😏 dunking, no “haha you forgot NULL.” Two real options. Spoken English a 0–2 YoE can hear once.
- Caption is 140–280 words, 6–10 sections, heavy line breaks. Required: hook, 💡 Answer, first-tool-is-incomplete (no dunking), teaching block (C1–C6), Interview Tip with ❌ / Say:, one-liner, In short, Save, comment keyword, keywords, hashtags. A 4-bullet stub is not a caption.
- This caption density is the only bar. Do not add a shorter Stories variant. Every post uses the same full teaching caption. Calibration: the git / `.gitignore` caption in `documents/instagram-daily-questions.md`.
- Topic picker (all five gates): noun a 0–2 YoE can read; everyday careless mistake; wrong first answer; two comment camps; teach in three spoken sentences. Fundamentals with a trap. One level above the fact everyone already recites (`IS NULL`). Not god-level.
- Frame must be a **mind game**: readable in 2 seconds on a phone, solvable in your head. Reject pen-and-paper frames (nested subqueries, truth tables, `NOT IN` + NULL). No specialist nouns (RAG, embeddings, LLM-as-Judge, Raft, CRDT).
- Frame is a short interview scene: situation, pressure, then `Will you use X or Y?` Not a one-liner. No stacked labels.
- Use one formation pattern per post (A–M in the guideline). Do not repeat yesterday’s pattern or topic lane.
- Voice: second person, one painful number or real system, one failure mode. No textbook “explain in detail”.
- Code gotchas: 3–5 lines, A/B/C only.
- Never ship a question body from the reference Reels or guideline examples. Those taught formation only. New noun, new trap, every post.
- Every time we hand Ashok a post: give **FRAME** and **CAPTION** as two copy-paste blocks. No extra lecture in between. He pastes them while creating the Reel.
- Do not build the daily generator until Ashok picks the ship path in the guideline (manual / CLI / scheduled agent).
